CHANGES IN VERSION 0.99.0
-------------------------

NEW FEATURES

* Initial Bioconductor submission
* Implemented basilisk-based Python environment management for TensorFlow/Keras
* Models now downloaded from Zenodo repository and cached locally
* Full support for Seurat v5 objects
* Integration with immApex for amino acid encoding

INFRASTRUCTURE CHANGES

* Removed direct keras/tensorflow R package dependencies
* Added basilisk for reproducible Python environment setup
* Models externalized to Zenodo (https://zenodo.org/records/14636032)
* Updated minimum R version to 4.4.0
* Improved documentation with roxygen2

ENCODING METHODS

* Deep learning autoencoders (VAE and AE) for TRA and TRB chains
* Support for Atchley factors (AF), Kidera factors (KF), and One-Hot Encoding (OHE)
* Geometric encoding using BLOSUM62 substitution matrix
* Models trained on 905,611 TRA and 1,276,462 TRB sequences
* Model architecture: 256-128-30-128-256 with batch normalization

MAIN FUNCTIONS

* maTrex() - Generate TCR embedding matrix from sequences
* runTrex() - Integrate embeddings into Seurat/SingleCellExperiment objects
* CoNGAfy() - Reduce data to representative cells per clonotype
* annotateDB() - Annotate TCR sequences using curated databases
* quietTCRgenes() - Remove TCR genes from variable features

DATABASE

* TCR-epitope annotation database compiled from VDJdb, McPAS-TCR, IEDB, and PIRD
* Support for edit distance-based fuzzy matching

DEPRECATED AND DEFUNCT

* Removed clonalCommunity() function
